# Issue 02 - analysis and actions

Status: analyzing (not started, no code change yet)

## Request

1. Choose the language inside the app instead of following Android.
2. The date shown on the photo must follow that choice.
3. Translate the menus into French, German and Spanish.

## Current state (verified in the code)

- `lib/l10n/app_en.arb` and `app_de.arb`: 155 keys each, template is `app_en.arb`
  (`l10n.yaml`). The three generated Dart files are checked in, so a new locale
  means one arb file plus its generated `app_localizations_<locale>.dart`.
- `lib/main.dart:185` `supportedLocales: [Locale('en'), Locale('de')]`. The
  `Global*Localizations` delegates are already registered, so a `Locale('fr')`
  needs no dependency change. `intl` is a dependency and
  `initializeDateFormatting()` runs in `app_initializer.dart:36`.
- No language setting exists anywhere: no config key, no field in
  `settings_screen.dart`. The app therefore shows English when Android runs in
  French or Spanish.
- `lib/ui/widgets/photo_info_overlay.dart:65-70` formats the photo date with
  `DateFormat.yMMMMd(Platform.localeName)`, i.e. the *platform* locale, not
  the locale of the app. This is the "only Android's default language is used
  to display the date" part of the report.
- `lib/ui/widgets/clock_overlay.dart:81` builds `HH:MM` by hand, so the clock
  is locale independent: no AM/PM, no locale date. A language choice does not
  change the clock unless the time format is locale driven too.

## Work to do

1. `language` config key (`''` = follow Android) in
   `domain/interfaces/config_provider.dart` and
   `infrastructure/services/json_config_service.dart`.
2. `MaterialApp.locale:` resolved from that key in `main.dart`, so every
   widget, the arb strings and `Localizations.localeOf(context)` follow it.
   `Intl.defaultLocale` has to be set too, because `DateFormat` without an
   explicit locale falls back on it.
3. `photo_info_overlay.dart`: format with the app locale from
   `Localizations.localeOf(context)` instead of `Platform.localeName`.
4. Language dropdown in the settings (general section) with "System" plus en,
   de, fr, es.
5. `app_fr.arb` and `app_es.arb` (155 keys each) and their generated Dart
   files; German already exists.

## Open point

The user has to say whether the clock follows the chosen language (12 h clock
and a localized date) or stays as it is (24 h, time only).

Reliability: 95 % for the code facts (read in the repository), the plan is
untested.
